[P_07_Battery_Briefings]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=LAMBERT - Fisher, I know you think the shortest distance to solving this problem is to go after Shetland, and you might be right. Unfortunately, the diplomatic situation surrounding the Walsh incident is not softening. We are less than twenty-four hours from open war on the Korean Peninsula. We've located the battery that launched the missile against the Walsh. If there is any credence to the North Korean claim that the launch was unintentional, we need to prove it...and fast.
Speech_0002L=GRIMSDOTTIR - I've been reverse engineering the data you recovered from Zherkezhi's computer in New York. Zherkezhi's algorithm is an advanced extrapolation of the Masse kernels made infinitely more complex by recursion through Dvorak. I think that if you can access the BIOS memory of the missile launchers at the battery, I should be able to ID a fingerprint that the algorithm would have left on the system.
Speech_0003L=REDDING - You'll be doing a HALO insertion into a forest two clicks east of the battery. You'll enter the battery's secure perimeter and infiltrate via the vehicle entrance. The battery itself has been around since World War Two, but intelligence and satellite imaging shows its been retrofitted several times since then. We have some limited mapping data... we don't know what you'll find.
Speech_0004L=MASON - Since the destruction of the Walsh, USS Ronald Reagan has assumed C and C duties for the Battle Group in the Yellow Sea. Our fleet is on Red Alert. In case of war, we are prepared to conduct precision sorties against high-value targets aimed at reducing North Korean coastal defenses for insertion behind their advancing front. If intelligence indicates that the Koreans are picking a fight, then it's a fight they'll get. Anyone in that battery when the whistle blows better find himself a tin hat and a bible.
Speech_0005L=OTOMO - Japanese I-SDF has been instrumental in determining that the missile that sank the Walsh was indeed fired from this battery.  You have the complete support of all branches of the Japanese Self Defense Force in order to determine the rationale for this insane move by the Korean aggressors. We do not have the capability to strike the facility directly, but I-SDF will use any means at our disposal to interfere with their capabilities in the event that our great American allies are forced to declare war.

[P_07_Battery_CheckLives]

[P_07_Battery_Checkpoints]

[P_07_Battery_Communications]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0003L=LAMBERT - Fisher... it's starting to look like war is unavoidable. JCOS is asking all sources for current Division level intelligence.
Speech_0004L=FISHER - So besides stopping World War Three, is there anything else I can do for you this evening?
Speech_0005L=LAMBERT - The base commander should have up to date intel about NKA divisional strength down the Kaesong-Munsan approach.
Speech_0006L=FISHER - I'll try to schedule an appointment with his secretary.
POPUPMESSAGE_0245=Determine if the Koreans intentionally launched the missile.
Speech_0099L=REDDING - Fisher, since everyone is asking everyone for intel, I'd love to have a few chips at the big table.
Speech_0100L=FISHER - What can I get you, Will?
Speech_0101L=REDDING - Looks like this battery has repair and maintenance capability for mechanized warfare support. Any shipping or repair logs you can recover would be a big help.
Speech_0102L=FISHER - I'll find what I can.
POPUPMESSAGE_0246=Recover the shipping and repair logs.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0103L=REDDING - Good work Fisher. Looks like they track shipping and repair through four separate departments.
Speech_0104L=FISHER - Gotta love military bureaucracy.
Speech_0105L=REDDING - See if you can get the logs from the other three.
Speech_0106L=FISHER - Now serving number 67.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0107L=REDDING - Good work Sam. One more shipping log to go and we'll have an accurate picture of their mechanized capabilities in the region.
Speech_0108L=FISHER - I'll find it.
Speech_0247L=(null)
Speech_0109L=REDDING - Good job, Sam. From the parts and transport requests, it looks like this facility is significantly more important than our latest estimates.
Speech_0110L=FISHER - Well you know me... always where the action is.
Speech_0235L=REDDING - Good work Sam... looks like you recovered the last of the logs.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0012L=LAMBERT - I see what you're thinking Fisher.
Speech_0013L=FISHER - If they're just going to throw protocol to the wind and leave the warhead case unlocked...
Speech_0014L=LAMBERT - Even detonating them won't destroy the battery.
Speech_0015L=FISHER - No, but it will make an awful big mess.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0017L=LAMBERT - Good work, Fisher.
Speech_0018L=FISHER - I'm uploading the arming sequence codes for Grim. Lambert, if worse comes to worst... and I'm still here.
Speech_0021L=LAMBERT - You don't even need to say it, Sam.
Speech_0221L=LAMBERT - Good thinking Fisher. Now if we have to, we can remote detonate those missiles and at least take the battery out of commission for a little while.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0022L=LAMBERT - Sweet Jesus Fisher... the NKA just committed... they're coming across the DMZ all along the thirty-eighth... we're at war.
Speech_0023L=FISHER - Why? We just found proof they didn't launch the missile.
Speech_0024L=LAMBERT - Good lord... speaking of missile launches... that battery just lit up like a smoker getting off an airplane...
Speech_0027L=FISHER - They're not targeting our ships are they?
Speech_0028L=LAMBERT - Active radar is up, and it looks like a launch is immanent. Fisher, I need you to abort that missile.
Speech_0029L=FISHER - You got it boss.
Note_0214L=War has broken out along the DMZ.
POPUPMESSAGE_0238=Stop the missile launch.
Speech_0224L=LAMBERT - Fisher... the NKA just spilled over into the DMZ... we're at war and it looks like that battery is about to launch more missiles. I need you to stop them.
Note_0225L=War has broken out along the DMZ.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0060L=GRIMSDOTTIR - That seals it... the missile came from here, but they didn't launch it intentionally.
Speech_0061L=FISHER - So, that's a good thing. We can avoid a war. 
Speech_0062L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Problem is that someone launched the missile intentionally.
Speech_0063L=FISHER - Isn't that someone Doug Shetland using Zherkezhi's algorithms?
Speech_0064L=GRIMSDOTTIR - That seems likely, but I still need to see if there's a Dvorak fingerprint on the BIOS of the launcher that fired the missile.
POPUPMESSAGE_0239=Tap the launcher BIOS to trace routing data for the Dvorak algorithm fragments.
Speech_0226L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, they didn't launch the missile intentionally. But we still need to see if we can find out who did, and where they did it from. Tap directly into the motherboard on the launcher that fired the missile.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0009L=LAMBERT - Good lord, Fisher... those numbers triple our best estimates...
Speech_0010L=FISHER - Damn... I know a lot of guys in 2.I.D. Lambert...
Speech_0011L=LAMBERT - They're good men... but I hope their life insurance policies are up to date.
Speech_0220L=LAMBERT - Fisher, that's the intel we needed about the Kaesong-Munsan approach... but it's not good. If this thing blows up in our faces, we're in big trouble.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0054L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Why did you do that? That technician could have answered some important questions...
Speech_0055L=FISHER - Like what?
Speech_0056L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Like if they launched the missile intentionally. See if he has any logs or journals backed up in his office.
Speech_0057L=FISHER - I'll take a peek.
Note_0215L=Check the senior technician's computer for classified reports
Speech_0227L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, you'll need to see if the technician keeps copies of his report backed up somewhere.
Note_0228L=Check the senior technician's computer for classified reports
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0030L=LAMBERT - Black hell... you're too late...
Speech_0031L=FISHER - The warhead won't arm until it's a few hundred meters from its target. If I can dig up the abort codes...
Speech_0032L=LAMBERT - Good thinking. Check launch control directly under the platform.
Speech_0033L=FISHER - I'm on my way.
Speech_0127L=LAMBERT - Make it fast Fisher... flight time on that missile is four minutes.
Speech_0128L=LAMBERT - Make it fast Fisher... flight time on that missile is three minutes.
Speech_0126L=LAMBERT - Make it fast Fisher... flight time on that missile is two minutes.
Speech_0129L=LAMBERT - Make it fast Fisher... flight time on that missile is ninety seconds.
Speech_0130L=LAMBERT - Make it fast Fisher... flight time on that missile is sixty seconds.
Speech_0131L=LAMBERT - Make it fast Fisher... flight time on that missile is thirty seconds.
Note_0216L=Upload the abort codes from the computer under the East launcher.
POPUPMESSAGE_0240=Acquire the missile abort codes.
Speech_0222L=LAMBERT - You were too late to stop the launch, but you can abort the missile from launch control underneath the platform. Hurry.
Note_0223L=Upload the abort codes from the computer under the East launcher.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0067L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Good work Sam, those are the abort codes.
Speech_0068L=FISHER - I still need to bypass the override circuit on the launcher itself.
Speech_0206L=FISHER - I still need to bypass the override circuit from the missile control room.
Speech_0069L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Hurry... the missile is closing on the USS Ronald Reagan at top speed.
Speech_0070L=FISHER - Um... hold on... did you just tell me I need to win one for the Gipper?
Speech_0071L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Uh... dude... what does that even mean?
Speech_0072L=FISHER - Uh... never mind... you're right Grim... I am old.
Note_0217L=Download the abort codes to the console in the missile control room.
POPUPMESSAGE_0241=Abort the missile.
Speech_0229L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Now we have the abort codes, you need to bypass the override circuits from the missile control room.
Note_0230L=Download the abort codes to the console in the missile control room.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0073L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Good job Sam... missile aborted.
Speech_0074L=FISHER - That's it... it's dust?
Speech_0075L=GRIMSDOTTIR - No, but the warhead can't arm. Even if it gets past the Reagan's phalanx it'll hit the hull and crumple like a beer can.
Speech_0076L=FISHER - Crumpling beer cans? That's what sailors are best at, I guess.
Speech_0077L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Very funny... you better hurry to the other launcher and tap the BIOS.
Speech_0078L=FISHER - Yeah, yeah, on my way.
Speech_0231L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Missile aborted. Get to the other launcher and tap the BIOS.
Speech_0079L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Very funny... you need to make your way to extraction.
Speech_0080L=FISHER - Right... on my way.
POPUPMESSAGE_0242=Exfiltrate to any available extraction point.
Speech_0232L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Missile aborted. Make your way to extraction.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0081L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Before you can tap into the BIOS, you'll need to open the casing.
Speech_0082L=FISHER - I didn't bring my crowbar.
Speech_0083L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Whatever... crowbars are for geeky video-game characters. Put the launcher into its maintenance position. There should be a switch in the control room directly beneath you.
Speech_0236L=GRIMSDOTTIR - You'll need to open the casing on the motherboard from the control room beneath you.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0086L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Alright, that opened the casing on the launcher's components. You can access the motherboard on the launcher itself and recover any routing data from the BIOS.
Speech_0233L=GRIMSDOTTIR - The casing is open. You can access the motherboard on the launcher itself and recover any routing data from the BIOS.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0087L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Good work Sam... I'm scanning the BIOS now... yep... that's a Dvorak fingerprint...
Speech_0088L=FISHER - Where did it come from? Hokkaido? The Displace offices?
Speech_0091L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Seoul.
Speech_0092L=FISHER - What? As in South Korea? Are you telling me the US just got drawn into a war protecting the people that sank the Walsh...
Note_0243L=War has broken out along the DMZ.
Speech_0093L=GRIMSDOTTIR - I can't trace it back farther than Seoul...
Speech_0094L=FISHER - Well, what do I do?
Speech_0260L=LAMBERT - Sweet Jesus Fisher... the NKA just committed... they're coming across the DMZ all along the thirty-eighth... we're at war.
Speech_0261L=FISHER - Why? We just found proof they didn't launch the missile.
Speech_0262L=LAMBERT - Good lord... speaking of missile launches... that battery just lit up like a smoker getting off an airplane...
Speech_0263L=FISHER - They're not targeting our ships are they?
Speech_0264L=LAMBERT - Active radar is up, and it looks like a launch is immanent. Fisher, I need you to abort that missile.
Speech_0265L=FISHER - You got it boss.
POPUPMESSAGE_0266=Stop the missile launch.
Speech_0097L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Jesus... well there's nothing you can do about it from there. Get to extraction.
Speech_0244L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Another complication. Looks like the launch order came through Seoul... I hope we're at war with the right people. Abort the missile launch in the East battery and get out of there. 
Speech_0267L=LAMBERT - Fisher... the NKA just spilled over into the DMZ... we're at war and it looks like that battery is about to launch more missiles. I need you to stop them.
Note_0268L=War has broken out along the DMZ.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0034L=LAMBERT - Fisher... remember what Mason said about a tin hat and a bible?
Speech_0035L=FISHER - You're kidding me...
Speech_0036L=LAMBERT - We just received a target report from an F-15 attached to Reagan Battle Group. They responded to the missile launch with GBU-28's directed at your location.
Speech_0037L=FISHER - A bunker buster?
Speech_0038L=LAMBERT - Two bunker busters...
Speech_0039L=FISHER - Hm... well my tin hat ain't gonna help, and I forgot my bible. What's the flight time?
Speech_0040L=LAMBERT - We're just getting the signal now...
Speech_0041L=LAMBERT - it's... my god... three minutes.
Speech_0202L=LAMBERT - it's... my god... two and a half minutes.
Speech_0203L=LAMBERT - it's... my god... two minutes.
Speech_0204L=LAMBERT - it's... my god... ninety seconds...
Speech_0205L=LAMBERT - it's... my god... one minute.
Speech_0042L=FISHER - Gotta run.
Speech_0111L=REDDING - Sam, I've got an exit scenario for you.
Speech_0112L=FISHER - Aw... I was just starting to like it here...
Speech_0113L=REDDING - Monitoring indicates that division is asking to move some coastal defense missiles south... there should be trucks leaving from the main garage.
Speech_0114L=FISHER - I think hitchhiking is illegal in North Korea.
Speech_0115L=REDDING - Then I'd recommend hiding under a tarp or strapping yourself to a chassis.
Speech_0207L=REDDING - Exit scenario, Sam.
Speech_0208L=FISHER - I'd love to hear it.
Speech_0209L=REDDING - Back out the way you came in... don't let anyone stop you.
Speech_0210L=REDDING - Back out the way you came in, or over the cliff from either launcher. Hurry.
Speech_0098L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Jesus... well for now, we still need to stop them from launching another missile... get to the other launcher.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0043L=LAMBERT - Fisher...
Speech_0044L=FISHER - I think I got turned around back there...
Speech_0045L=LAMBERT - Sam... I...
Speech_0046L=FISHER - Yeah... I know...
Speech_0047L=LAMBERT - I can... I can try to patch you through to--
Speech_0048L=FISHER - No. We haven't really been talking...
Speech_0049L=LAMBERT - It's never too late to start.
Speech_0050L=FISHER - Ha. I think we might have just found the exception to that rule...
Speech_0051L=LAMBERT - Sam... I'm sorry... I--
Speech_0052L=FISHER - Don't be. Mission complete, right.
Speech_0053L=LAMBERT - Mission Complete
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0116L=O'DELL - And... on the front lines, allied forces continue their round-the-clock vigil of North Korean activity. It has long been known that the North Korean invasion strategy aims at a rapid and devastating push for the South Korean Capitol of Seoul. If such an advance were successful any hope of a quick resolution to hostilities in the Asian subcontinent would be jeopardized.
Speech_0118L=O'DELL - In other news... national home renovation and hardware supplier Handy Hardwood launched its official Support Our Troops campaign today. Customers are invited to come and fill out cards and letters of encouragement to our nations fighting men and women. For each card filled out, Handy Hardwood offers lumber and materials valued at ten dollars. Give our boys a hand, and they'll give you wood.
Speech_0119L=O'DELL - We have reports coming in now from all along the DMZ of a massive North Korean advance. Fighting is on a reportedly unprecedented scale, with US and South Korean troops ...quote- laying down a tidal wave of fire ...unquote- against the juggernaut advance of the NKA.
Speech_0120L=O'DELL - Field reports indicate that entire Divisions of NKA infantry and armor have overrun US and South Korean defenses, and have continued directly toward Seoul. Other sources report limited but successful rear echelon offensives by remnant allied troops who were left behind by the first echelon NKA advance whose sole objective seems to be to capture Seoul at any cost.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0181L=GEN SOLDIER - Reminder to all personnel. Food and water rationing in effect until further notice.
Speech_0182L=GEN SOLDIER - Corporal Dak-po report to Receiving. Corporal Dak-po to Receiving.
Speech_0183L=GEN SOLDIER - We are the fierce and loyal siblings of a great and indefatigable nation.
Speech_0184L=GEN SOLDIER - Reminder to all enlisted personnel. Tomorrow is new toothbrush day.
Speech_0185L=GEN SOLDIER - Reminder. No memos are to be posted on facility corkboards without approval from Warrant Officer Pok.
Speech_0186L=GEN SOLDIER - Technician Lop-Pong report to loading bay four. Technician Lop-Pong to loading bay four.
Speech_0187L=GEN SOLDIER - Remember, every bullet is manufactured with extra vengeance. Destroy the enemy hatefully.
Speech_0188L=GEN SOLDIER - All personnel are reminded to return their dishes to the kitchen after meal time.
Speech_0189L=GEN SOLDIER - Under rationing constraints, enlisted personnel ranked corporal or lower are reminded they may only shower on Monday and Thursday.
Speech_-001L=(null)
